  "finalText": "Nothing built; use a circle path via shape instead of an ellipse.\nI built the NOVA logo reveal as a 4 s, 60 fps comp. I checked it on a six-frame contact sheet; I didn't run the critic, a motion check or a collision check.\n\n- **Look:** navy background (`#0B1630`) with a single mint accent (`#2EE6A6`). The wordmark is white Inter ExtraBold.\n- **0.3–1.4 s, mark:** **Mark Circle** draws itself as a ring, then **Mark Slash** draws diagonally across it.\n- **1.5–2.3 s, wordmark:** **Wordmark** slides out from behind the mark. It sits in a clipped group (**Wordmark Mask**), so it emerges from the mark's edge instead of fading in. The ease is Expo Out.\n- **2.4–3.0 s, tagline:** **Tagline** (\"Money, made simple\") fades in underneath in the accent color.\n- **3.0–4.0 s, hold:** the full lockup holds still for a full second.\n\nThe tagline is small next to the wordmark, and the lockup sits slightly right of center, so say if you want either adjusted. I can also add a subtle pulse on the mark when the wordmark lands, or bump the tagline size."
